From ae854481439d86349132d902bc39318c9ab9c2c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MOTOR-44 (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:59:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cosmetic filters: keep [style] hide selectors out of
 stylesheets

A hide selector that tests the style attribute (div[style^="..."]) in any
stylesheet makes Blink serialize the inline style of every element it
matches, on every style recalc (ElementRuleCollector, RuleSet::
HasBucketForStyleAttribute). The default lists bring 23 such generic rules
to every page; in MotionMark Multiply that is 22 % of the renderer main
thread.

Take those selectors out of the hide stylesheets (all four paths: generic,
force, class/id, aggressive) and hand them to content_cosmetic.ts, which
matches them on added nodes and in a sweep every second, and marks the
matches with a random attribute hidden by one user stylesheet rule.
Standard mode keeps the first-party check of the queues; force and
aggressive selectors skip it, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2h13FSCtFp8GwQLUyv
